        "original_id": "d7670ac0-fe21-5b4f-a080-b34881622fdc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Public Television 19, Inc., Avila University\n- TV Stations: KCPT, KCTV\n- Radio Stations: KTBG\n- TV Programs: Check, Please!\n- People: Tim Johnson\n- Places: Kansas City, Missouri, Kansas City, Kansas, Union Hill, Blue Valley, East 31st Street, 23rd Street, Stark Avenue\n\nFacts:\n- In 1999, Tim Johnson was hired by Avila University in Kansas City, Missouri, to start the school's football program.\n- In 2009, Check, Please! began airing in Kansas City on KCPT.\n- KCPT is owned by Public Television 19, Inc.\n- KCPT maintains studio facilities on East 31st Street in Kansas City, Missouri's Union Hill section.\n- KCPT shares its studio facilities with sister adult album alternative radio station KTBG (90.9 FM).\n- KCPT's studios are adjacent to the transmitter tower of CBS affiliate KCTV.\n- KCPT's transmitter is located near 23rd Street and Stark Avenue in Kansas City, Missouri's Blue Valley section.\n- KCTV is virtual channel 5 and broadcasts on UHF digital channel 24.\n- KCTV is a CBS-affiliated television station licensed to Kansas City, Missouri, and it also serves Kansas City, Kansas.",
